From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:41:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Take the IR TX clock from the 24 MHz
 system clock

IRTX_CLK_REG selects 000 = SYS_CLK24M in the A733 manual. The driver
maps 000 to the 32 kHz oscillator, so at the reset value the clock tree
reports irtx at 32768 Hz while the hardware runs from 24 MHz, and an IR
TX driver would compute its carrier from a rate about 730 times too
low.

Map 000 to the 24 MHz system clock. 001 = PERI1_600M and 010 = DCXO are
unchanged.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the IR transmitter on mux value 0 finished in
the time of a 24 MHz source, not of the 32 kHz oscillator, and the clock
tree showed sys-24M as its parent.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
index ee5925122e0e..1ec59f5f0df4 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -1123,7 +1123,7 @@ static SUNXI_CCU_M_DATA_WITH_MUX_GATE(irrx_clk, "irrx", irrx_parents, 0x1000,
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_irrx_clk, "bus-irrx", apb0_hws, 0x1004, BIT(0), 0);
 
 static const struct clk_parent_data irtx_parents[] = {
-	{ .fw_name = "losc"},
+	{ .hw = &sys_24M_clk.hw },
 	{ .hw = &pll_periph1_600M_clk.hw },
 	{ .fw_name = "hosc"},
 };
